      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hello ​<user-mention data-id=\"108566\">@Profanity</user-mention>,</p><p>I recommend referring to the LSM303AGR integration available in STM32CubeF4: Link (<a href=\"https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeF4/tree/89e6d4466578bc9eab83de8fcd1e397ceb5e5cc9/Projects/STM32F411E-Discovery/Demonstrations\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>As ​<user-mention data-id=\"72982\">@Dor_RH</user-mention> said, have you tried ST’s provided example?</p><p>What hardware are you using?</p><p> </p><blockquote><p>The magnetometer doesn’t start over I2C</p></blockquote><p>Have you checked hardware connections?</p><p>Correct pullups?</p><p>Correct slave address, and correctly presented in the software?</p><p>Have you used an oscilloscope and/or logic analyser to see what’s actually happening on the bus?</p><p> </p><blockquote><p>doesn’t output data via UART</p></blockquote><p>The LSM303AGR doesn’t have a UART.</p><p> </p><p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/community-guidelines-160/how-to-write-your-question-to-maximize-your-chances-to-find-a-solution-118622\"></oembed></p><p> </p></div>"
